                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "spB9o",
                      "name": "Notes",
                      "width": 640,
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 12,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "X7Mxke",
                          "name": "Notes heading",
                          "fill": "#1A1400",
                          "content": "Notes",
                          "fontFamily": "Schibsted Grotesk",
                          "fontSize": 20,
                          "fontWeight": "700"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "Zr9pz",
                          "name": "Notes body",
                          "fill": "#2A2A2A",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Two simulated chemicals on a grid one-third the screen's size (Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion): one is fed in, the other consumes it and multiplies. Feed and kill rates decide dots that split, worms or coral; colour comes from the second chemical's amount plus a fixed paper grain.\n\nIdle: 200 steps a second. The rates drift slowly and a small seed lands in a bare patch every 2.5 s, so dots keep splitting. A higher kill rate keeps a clearing behind the card.\nChecking: feed rises in rings sent out from the card every 1.6 s; the pattern thickens and darkens.\nRefused: kill rate rises in a circle widening from the card; the pattern dies back to the edges.\n\nBone #E9E1CF, oxblood #5A1018, ink #1E0A0C, Plex #E5A00D. Font: GT Sectra italic.\nCost: about 11 ms a frame idle, 13 checking, drawn at half resolution.\nNext: move the simulation into a WebGL shader for a finer grid.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "Schibsted Grotesk",
                          "fontSize": 15,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
